# Inert registered Finance candidate consumption (source/pure only)

Based on1cfd7cd, no DB/SQL execution, constructors, held sources, providers or route activation. Candidate membership is not Finance/PMO visibility or whole-worklist completion.

ReaderAdmission.admit now takes the actual registered worklist and its exact Finance row object, one binding per invocation. The closed producer consumer rechecks marker registry identity, exact row membership, fresh actor/PK/normalized keys/default/raw connection and original Template.case witness before any Finance query/helper. Existing phase cap is charged; mismatch poisons original/current entries. There is no naked tuple fallback. Existing ledger per-binding processing/identity permits, shared-run caps/global bytes, sticky errors and native PPE/recipient ordering remain.

A single closed full binding-context EXISTS is used by identity, initial/final SIZE, COUNT, CLASS and TRANSFER. It pins all nine original binding/run/Version/template/document/run-case/tenant/synthetic values and separately joins the actual Template.case UUID. Run case is not equated with Template or Document case. COUNT/CLASS include the context predicate inside the admitted CASE before guarded array length/expansion; distinct guard-miss vs valid-empty semantics remain. Initial/final SIZE uses the same EXISTS in its WHERE. TRANSFER retains own snapshot metadata predicates and now the same context. No post-transfer check is represented as a pre-transfer guard.

Six new pure checks cover registered/forged membership, shared run/distinct cases, context mismatch poisoning, actual admit call order, all-phase fixed SQL/parameter shapes and modeled Template.case guard misses with no decode. Existing Finance phase tests use an explicit stub consumer to isolate their original phase/cap assertions; the new tests execute the real producer/consumer code with fake scalar stores. These are not SQL evaluation or native permission tests. Original nested CASE, conditional byte transfer, fresh codec, no nonstatement snapshot path and unchanged policy descriptor remain.

Later stage: private one-use Finance native-denial outcomes are implemented only at three fixed helper callsites (see template-finance-native-denial803-inert.md). Engineering failures still poison; no public hidden/visible aggregation or PMO outcome protocol exists. Full closure/visibility orchestration remains blocked. Native SQL/grant equivalence and real own-write/concurrency tests are UNRUN; no broad security or full milestone claim. Outer selected-owner closure requirements still narrow admission compared with arbitrary native template-reader calls.
